# tiny5: an example frit at the small end of the range, Tiny5 Mono at its
# own 6x9 cell (vtium/vtium#197). It shows how small a frit's cell can
# go, 6 pixels wide being the narrowest a frit may state. It is never a
# default: vtium draws it only where font-name or a profile names it.
# Tiny5 Mono is a pixel font whose capitals are 5 pixels tall, drawn on a
# 6-pixel advance with 7 rows above the baseline and 2 below. At 6x9 a
# 320x240 panel holds 53x26 cells and a 640x480 one 106x53, where the
# built-in Unscii-8's 8x8 gives 40x30 and 80x60. It holds all of ASCII,
# Latin-1, code page 437, Greek, Armenian, box drawing, blocks and
# Braille, most of Cyrillic and of Symbols for Legacy Computing, 4,882
# characters in all, each one cell wide. vtium ships this frit, never the
# font: the helper draws from the BDF file the machine holds, and leaves
# the source out when the file is missing.
#
# The frit has one source. The console draws a character Tiny5 Mono
# lacks in the built-in font for the cell (ADR-1200 D7), Unscii-8 here,
# centered in the 6x9 cell with a column cut off each side, so the frit
# names no builtin: line. Unscii-8 could not be a second source anyway:
# its 8x8 cell does not fit in Tiny5 Mono's 6x9, and the helper refuses a
# bitmap source whose cell does not fit the first source's.
#
# Box drawing, blocks, Braille, sextants, octants and Legacy Computing
# draw as vtium's sprites, the default glyph-source, which line up across
# cells. Tiny5 Mono's own box and block glyphs fill the cell too;
# glyph-source=font draws them instead.
#
# Bold is weak at this size: vtium draws bitmap bold by widening each row
# by a pixel, and with 5-pixel glyphs and a 1-pixel gap that fills the
# counters of letters such as x and 0.
#
# Licences, as each source's documentation gives them:
# - Tiny5 Mono: SIL OFL 1.1, "Copyright 2026 The Tiny5 Mono Project
#   Authors (https://github.com/Gissio/font_Tiny5Mono)", as the BDF's
#   COPYRIGHT property gives it; it names no Reserved Font Name. The
#   repository's OFL.txt still carries its template's placeholder
#   copyright line.

name=tiny5
cell=6x9
license=OFL-1.1

# Tiny5 Mono's BDF, the font at its own cell. Written against
# github.com/Gissio/font_Tiny5Mono at 7d30f9e887fdb29e0b951e92493822afba5f70a7
# (version 3.000), file fonts/bdf/Tiny5Mono.bdf, SHA-256
# 33a935687277817534ddcc1decf586d977cee211550f611ba4bb4365e99755d3.
# No Arch or AUR package installs it: download that file from the
# repository at that commit, check its SHA-256, and copy it to the path
# below, readable by every account, since the helper reads it as nobody
# before login. vtium-vitrify reads the file as published: it takes the
# character set from the XLFD name, as the file has no CHARSET_REGISTRY
# property, and leaves out the 73 small capitals of ENCODING -1, which the
# file's CHARS line does not count.
# No cover= line: every glyph the file holds is one cell wide and drawn in
# the cell, and the frit has no other source to share codepoints with.
source=bdf:/usr/local/share/fonts/misc/Tiny5Mono.bdf
